        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7809050b-f643-5612-97a2-1f897bfc194b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2, Douglas SBD Dauntless, Curtiss SB2C Helldiver, Curtiss XSB3C\n- Companies: Douglas Aircraft, Curtiss-Wright\n- Organizations: United States Navy, U.S. Navy\n- Events: invasion of Lae-Salamaua\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n\nFacts:\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2 was damaged off Lae, New Guinea by Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown.\n- Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless, a World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber, from 1940 through 1944.\n- The Curtiss SB2C Helldiver replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in U.S. Navy service.\n- The Curtiss XSB3C was a proposed Curtiss-Wright development of the Curtiss SB2C Helldiver submitted to meet a U.S. Navy requirement for a new dive bomber to replace the SB2C in service.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "43e7a92a-eac8-59c3-87af-18d60d866dda",
        "text": "Page: Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2. Sentence: On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, \"Tama Maru No. 2\" was damaged by Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS \"Lexington\" and USS \"Yorktown\" off Lae, New Guinea.\nPage: Douglas SBD Dauntless. Sentence: The Douglas SBD Dauntless was a World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber that was manufactured by Douglas Aircraft from 1940 through 1944.\nPage: Curtiss SB2C Helldiver. Sentence: It replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in US Navy service.\nPage: Curtiss XSB3C. Sentence: The Curtiss XSB3C was a proposed development by Curtiss-Wright of the Curtiss SB2C Helldiver dive bomber, submitted to meet a U.S. Navy requirement for a new dive bomber to replace the SB2C in service.",
